<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fernando Henrique Cardoso</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1931">1931</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fernando Henrique Cardoso is a Brazilian sociologist and politician who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> from 1995 to 2002. As finance minister in 1993–1994 he introduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/real-plan">Real Plan</a>, which ended decades of hyperinflation, and its success carried him to the presidency. In office he privatised state companies and stabilised the economy; earlier, as a scholar, he had helped develop dependency theory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fernando-henrique-cardoso.jpg" alt="Fernando Henrique Cardoso" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Agência Brasil · CC BY 3.0 br · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fernando_Henrique_Cardoso_(1999).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
